Patch 2914: a fragment program's inline constants are walked out of guest memory once per batch (FPK_MEMO, default on,
FPK_MEMO=0 off; experiment).

rsx_fp_extract_consts ran per draw at record time and again per draw at replay (patch 2058 FPK_REPLAY, which overwrites
the record-time values), walking the whole program each time: rsx_fp_extract_consts 2.4% + rsx_fp_read_word 0.7% of the
FIFO thread in a 2 vs 2 with about 4,500 draws a frame (sampling profile). With FPK_REPLAY on (the default) the
record-time walk is skipped, and the replay keeps each program's constants in a 256-entry table for the batch
(s_fpk_batch, bumped in render_frame_prepare) and copies them to the next draw of the same program. Every draw of one
program in a batch read the same memory at replay, so the values are the same as before.

Tested (Experiments workbench, heavy 2 vs 2 on Hidden Leaf at 4K, PIPE=1, alternating): FPK_MEMO on 27.11 and 28.29
flips/s (FTL draw 24.5, 21.7), off 27.49 and 25.01 (25.1, 26.9): a small gain within the run-to-run spread. Picture correct.

